1
00:00:00,750 --> 00:00:05,446
A data center never sleeps. Neither can its power.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:13,459
Electricity arrives from the grid, and a transformer steps it down to about 400 volts.

3
00:00:14,125 --> 00:00:17,762
Then it meets the low-voltage switchgear.

4
00:00:20,375 --> 00:00:25,893
Inside, a main breaker lets power onto heavy copper busbars.

5
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:31,625
Feeder breakers share it out: to the UPS, the cooling, the server racks.

6
00:00:31,625 --> 00:00:36,000
When a cable faults, only the breaker closest to it trips.

7
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:38,623
Everything else stays on.

8
00:00:39,125 --> 00:00:41,750
And if the grid goes dark?

9
00:00:41,750 --> 00:00:47,234
The UPS batteries hold the servers while the generator starts.

10
00:00:47,250 --> 00:00:53,687
The switchgear changes source, never connecting both at once, and power flows again.

11
00:00:54,125 --> 00:00:58,935
Switch. Protect. Transfer. Every second, of every day.
